260
00:39:37.290 --> 00:39:45.160
Etan (Nimbus): To be based on SSZ. So it's just a block hash now, it's not transactions, not receipts.

261
00:39:46.020 --> 00:39:49.189
Etan (Nimbus): Anymore, so that it stays simple.

262
00:39:49.540 --> 00:40:03.230
Etan (Nimbus): It also has a way smaller dependency list now than it used to have. The main benefit here is that, again, for the users who are accessing it, they can

263
00:40:03.270 --> 00:40:10.770
Etan (Nimbus): prove individual fields of the block without downloading the full header. And also for the CL,

264
00:40:10.770 --> 00:40:29.630
