265
00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:34.960
Etan (Nimbus): I think there's also some interactions with Yatex TopUpSync,

266
00:40:35.970 --> 00:40:39.259
Etan (Nimbus): Well, yeah, the idea here is just change the block hash.

267
00:40:39.670 --> 00:40:44.629
Etan (Nimbus): To the same way how we hash it on the CL and align those two.

268
00:40:47.020 --> 00:40:53.729
Etan (Nimbus): Then, let me check the comments real quick. There is some similar EIP problem as if you want to use priority fee.

