273
00:41:30.300 --> 00:41:38.619
Etan (Nimbus): You will have to download both of them to have a trust-minimized way to verify that the data is correct that you receive from the server.

274
00:41:38.940 --> 00:41:46.689
Etan (Nimbus): Yes, it's in the response, but it's not committed on-chain. Like, the server can just put whatever data is in there, and you have no way to verify.

275
00:41:46.980 --> 00:41:51.410
Etan (Nimbus): Unless you download both. And then this should take into account…

