01:04:56.750 --> 01:05:16.640
jochem-brouwer: Ansgar, so that's very funny. So, this EIP, we know the Boom filters, they were, so these are the locked Bloom filters. They are not, either not being used anymore, or, like, not very useful anymore, so we should remove them. Well, what is removing means, that is something that we can talk about. What was very,

427
01:05:16.640 --> 01:05:21.099
jochem-brouwer: surprised about is that EIP7906, which is the SSZ block.

428
01:05:21.280 --> 01:05:40.680
jochem-brouwer: Execution blocks is, well, this is exactly what Tony is asking right now. I was surprised that, this is part of the SCC Execution EIP also, but I still want to propose this EIP, in,

429
01:05:40.760 --> 01:05:52.269
jochem-brouwer: individually, because if Etan's EIP does not, if Etan's EIP does not make it, I think they support that EIP, but if it does not make it, then we can still deprecate slash remove the logs bloom.

430
01:05:52.270 --> 01:06:11.490
jochem-brouwer: EIP 8304, which is the Justice Log and Transaction Index. This actually, it says it will not remove the Bloom filters itself, but I think this specific EIP, which removes the Bloom filters, works perfectly together with that EIP.

431
01:06:11.490 --> 01:06:25.360
jochem-brouwer: So this is why I'm proposing it. It's a very simple change. The Bloomfields are not being used anymore, but clients still… all the clients are still re-executing this, and therefore calculating it. That's a waste of energy, and clients can use that elsewhere. So, let's remove funds.

432
01:06:25.750 --> 01:06:26.520
jochem-brouwer: Thank you.

433
01:06:29.670 --> 01:06:30.500
Ansgar Dietrichs: Sounds good.

