458
01:09:01.479 --> 01:09:06.029
Kevaundray Wedderburn: run this library, so, like, the Blake2F equivalent library.

459
01:09:06.599 --> 01:09:13.129
Kevaundray Wedderburn: Whereas with ZKVMs, you'd be repricing it, based on prover costs, if we introduce prover costs.

460
01:09:20.039 --> 01:09:20.769
Kevaundray Wedderburn: Yeah, I was.

461
01:09:20.770 --> 01:09:31.030
Toni Wahrstätter: I was more thinking of just repricing it based on how much it would cost with EVM code, and under the hood, clients could basically change nothing.

462
01:09:32.830 --> 01:09:40.870
Kevaundray Wedderburn: I think that does introduce some complexity, right? Because you'll be repricing it based off of a contract that's not…

463
01:09:41.010 --> 01:09:45.229
